{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And the rain was not poured on the earth.</b> It did not say לא ירד (it did not come down) but rather לא נתך (it was not poured), to teach that after it came down from the sky it stood between the sky and the earth. And so the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded that they stood between the sky and the earth for forty-one years until the time of Joshua; this is what is said (Joshua 10:11): ״וה׳ השליך עליהם אבנים גדולות מן השמים״ — and HaShem cast great stones upon them from the sky, etc. And Ezekiel the prophet told them to fall, as is said (Ezekiel 13:11): ״ואתנה אבני אלגביש תפלנה״. And they are called אבני אלגביש because they stood upon גב איש — the back of the man, which is Moses, as is said (Numbers 12:3): ״והאיש משה״ — and the man Moses. And they did not reach the earth until a later time. And because the hailstones shine like pearls, therefore they were called thus, for so you find regarding pearls (Job 28:18): ״ראמות וגביש לא יזכר״. And the sounds (קולות) too were suspended, and when did they come down? In the days of Elisha, as is said (II Kings 7:6): ״וה׳ השמיע אל מחנה ארם קול רכב וקול סוס קול חיל גדול״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The Hebrew מ״א שנה is read as מ״א = 41; the argument turns on reading גביש (hailstone) as גב איש (the back of the man), both rendered literally here."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:22.632462532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}